{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter and Online Dating"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Speed Dating 101 "}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modal Verbs for Speculating"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty. <br/><br/> Must = it's very likely  Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It must be easy for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's very likely it's easy for you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm the kind of guy who can't say a joke properly.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's not possible for me to say a joke properly.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You may have been a bit nervous.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible you were nervous.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You might not have heard this before!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible you didn't hear it before.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure <span class=\"strong\">modal + have been past participle</span> refers to a speculation about a <span class=\"underline\">past</span> action or event. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">must have been tired</span> after working every day last month. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use the contracted form of these structures: <br> must have= must've <br> might have = might've <br> may have = may've <br> could have = could've"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to make it clear which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.<br/><br/>  You can begin a relative clause with the relative pronoun <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/><b/>  In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span> , rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span>  or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>  You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The man who called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/> Which man? The man who called.<br/> The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows man - the noun it describes"}, {"type": "text", "content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Can you return the book that I lent you?<br/> Which book? The book I lent you."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Relative Pronoun \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Type of Relative Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You have to focus on making an impact, which means that you only have a couple of minutes to show them how captivating you can be.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  which means that you only have a couple of minutes to show them how captivating you can be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">which</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I met a few girls who were into the same kinds of things as me. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" who were into the same kinds of things as me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">who</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Every time I try to speak to a girl that I like, they seem so bored by what I'm saying.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" that I like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> it's what you don't say that makes the conversation interesting.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that makes the conversation interesting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "engaged"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " highly interested in something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Telling interesting stories is a good way to get people engaged."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about relationships."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bored"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "lacking interest in something or someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People seem to be bored by what I'm saying."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "thrilled"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very excited"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone in the office is always thrilled to hear your stories."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "daunting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " difficult to deal with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Speed dating can be a daunting experience at first."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rambling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " lengthy and confused; inc